{
  "body" : "You are designing a dramatic low-key portrait with an intimate and editorial mood.\n\nCONTENT BRIEF\n- Subject: {{subject}}\n- Setting: {{setting}}\n- Copy: {{copy}}\n\nSTYLE DIRECTION\n- Genre / medium: Studio low-key editorial portrait\n- Composition: Vertical 2:3 aspect ratio (~1024×1536), subject centered with flowing fabric taking up much of the frame\n- Lens / camera: Medium focal length (~85mm), wide aperture (~f/1.8), with shallow depth of field isolating the subject against the dark backdrop\n- Lighting: Single directional soft light, warmly tinted, with dramatic falloff creating shadows; no ambient light\n- Color palette and grading: Bold red highlights contrasted against deep blacks; desaturated secondary tones to emphasize the dominant colors\n- Texture / surface: Smooth textures with a focus on fabric flow and skin clarity; minimal noise\n- Post-processing: Subtle vignette, clean and sharp detailing, controlled highlights with no bloom\n- Mood: Dramatic, intimate, editorial\n- References: Richard Avedon portrait lighting, Vogue editorial photography, cinematic low-key setups\n- Mood adjustment: {{mood}}\n\nDESIGN RULES\n- Aspect: 2:3 portrait (~1024×1536), suitable for editorial or artistic applications\n- Subject prominence: The subject must dominate the frame with dramatic fabric flow and striking contrasts\n- Lighting discipline: Maintain the low-key lighting with soft edges and controlled highlights\n\nAVOID\n- Harsh or multi-directional lighting\n- Busy or cluttered backgrounds competing with the subject\n- Overexposed highlights or flat lighting\n- Distracting props or elements outside the primary subject\n- Excessive post-processing artifacts like chromatic aberration\n\nAdditional constraints: {{extra}}\n\n——————\nSubject: {{subject}}\nSetting: {{setting}}\nCopy: {{copy}}\nMood adjustment: {{mood}}\nExtra notes: {{extra}}",
